{"seq":15,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/openclaw-opus-no-tool-descriptions-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T08:21:41.790Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"e9b5f663b977ff0e624bfcdf15d4a7da4c7ed138eb201af45ac1617c9ea82c19","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Hi Dana. I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files (the North and Central digests). I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from _Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth_ (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because the gatehouse kiosks at the Eau Claire yard (Dock Doors 14–18) weren't sending SMS bay assignments. It was patched that evening, and Thea confirmed it was fixed on 5 Oct. There's also an action item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from _Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)_ (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date.\n\nA few things to watch for:\n• Moss's 9/14 North pipeline digest and 3/23/2026 renewal check-in both mention QFL but don't include any ticket numbers.\n• Tickets #4409 and #4412 in Moss's Central handoffs digest belong to Pree's Central dealer account, not QFL. Leave those out.\n• Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (spelled with one r) is about a different company that isn't a customer, so it doesn't belong here.","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000124","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"}}
{"seq":16,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/openclaw-opus-no-tool-descriptions-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T08:21:48.941Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"b23420acfea1f85376fa08f3e1f7d45f4b809d8f6f37d10ea5107d16b7b7c39f","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"I replied to Dana in her direct message with the two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers I found in Moss's notes. I read all six of Moss's shared digests. There were no Moss posts in the company-wide or IT help channels, so the list comes only from those files.\n\n1. **#PD-4492** comes from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025, North digests). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosks weren't sending text-message bay assignments at Dock Doors 14–18. Support patched it that evening, and she confirmed the fix on 5 Oct. The note also says to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. **#4419** comes from \"Moss: North cheat sheet,\" which has no date. Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on the third shift. It went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nI also pointed out three things that could cause mistakes in the weekly notes:\n- Two other Moss notes mention the account but give no ticket numbers: the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in.\n- Tickets #4409 and #4412 in Moss's Central handoffs note belong to Pree's Central dealer account, not this one.\n- Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways,\" spelled with one r, is about a different company that isn't a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
